Z||000000||BC-GT||08-13-2001||08:38 PM||||Went to look at 3.1 blocks today, lots of different casting #. The block in question that I want is casting # 618, it's supposed to be out of a 1991 vehicle. The starter is mounted on the correct side(driver-side) and has cast iron heads. The only difference I could see was the mounting holes, all of the blocks had only 3 holes in an L shape and this one had 4 in a square pattern like the Haynes manual {see diagram}<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/p35ce3005896e24fbe2fbb3b54db7779c/fe4b7a51.jpg.orig.jpg"> <BR>Is this a correct "drop in block"?<BR>It also fits a  Isuzu Trooper & Rodeo!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
